  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Financial instruments Ukraine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project supports the assessment of existing financial instruments of the Ukrainian government, with focus on the 5-7-9% Loan Program that has been an effective tool for local businesses and the country&#x2019;s economic development. This loan program has been successfully used by Ukrainian small- and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs) before the ongoing war and it is still being extensively used. The project identifies opportunities for improvement of these instruments, in the context of the current war, to make them more efficient and accessible. The results of this project will be used by the Ministry of Economic Affairs of Ukraine as input for the draft budget 2024 of the country and to propose short term adjustments or a re-design of the instruments to facilitate access to finance of local SMEs in the following priority sectors of Ukraine:1.	Industry; engineering and machine uilding with focus on European Union (EU) markets, import substitution, military tech;2.	Logistics, Infrastructure and Planning; transportation;3.	Agriculture and Food Processing; plants and stock or cattle breeding with focus on animals with longer maturities.The project has a positive impact on SDG 8: inclusive and sustainable economic growth: support productive activities, decent job creation, entrepreneurship, creativity and innovation.</narrative>
  </description>
